.TH DHISBENCH 8 "2026-10-26"
.SH NAME
dhisbench \- benchmark Diablo history adds and lookups
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dhisbench
[
.B \-f
.I historyfile
]
[
.B \-af
.I forks
]
[
.B \-ac
.I count
]
[
.B \-lf
.I forks
]
[
.B \-lc
.I count
]
[
.BR \-F [ l | s ]
]
[
.B \-h
.I hsize
]
[
.B \-m
.I statsfile
]
[
.B \-C
.I diablo.config
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I dhisbench
measures history performance: it starts processes that add made-up
entries to a history file and processes that look entries up, and prints
the number of operations and the time they took.  At least one of
.B \-af
or
.B \-lf
is required.
.PP
The add processes write made-up entries, so adds need a scratch history
file given with
.BR \-f ;
dhisbench refuses to add to the configured dhistory.  Lookups alone use
dhistory (read-only) when \-f is not given.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-f " historyfile"
The history file to use.  Required when adds are requested with \fB\-af\fP;
dhisbench refuses to add to the configured dhistory.
.TP
.BI \-af " forks" " \fR,\fP \-ac " count
Number of add processes, and entries each adds.
.TP
.BI \-lf " forks" " \fR,\fP \-lc " count
Number of lookup processes, and lookups each does.
.TP
.B \-F
Fast adds: no locking and no duplicate check.  \fB\-Fl\fP: no locking
only; \fB\-Fs\fP: no duplicate check only.
.TP
.BI \-h " hsize"
Hash table size for a new file (power of 2, 256k to 128m).
.TP
.BI \-m " statsfile"
File for the shared statistics (default path_run/dhisbench.map).
.TP
.BI \-C " diablo.config"
Use this diablo.config instead of the default.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
dhisbench -f /var/tmp/dhistory.bench -af 4 -ac 100000 -lf 4
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
dilookup(8),
diload(8),
diablo-files(5)
